THIS AGREEMENT is between the City of Cheyenne(hereinafter referred toas Owner)on behalf
of the Cheyenne Laramie County GIS Cooperative and Aero-Graphics, Inc.(hereinafter referred
to as Provider);
WITNESSETH:
WHEREAS, Owner intends to have Provider perform aerial photography and Li DAR services for
the2019Aerial Imagery and Li DAR Project(hereinafter referred to as the Project); and,
WHEREAS, Owner requires certain professional services in connection with the Project
(here in after referred to as the Services); and,
WHEREAS, Provider is prepared to provide such Services;
NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the promises contained herein, the parties hereto agree
as follows:
ARTICLE1-ARTICLE EFFECTIVE DATE
The effective date of this Agreement shall be February1,2019orwhenfully executed.
ARTICLE2-SCOPE OF WORK AND TIME FOR PERFORMANCE
Providcr shall pcrform thc Scrviccs describcd in thc Scopc of Work attachcd hcrcto as
AttachmentA, which is incorporated by reference as part of this Agreement.Providers hall deliver
all data collected pursuant to Attachment A to the Owner by December31,2019.
ARTICLE3-COMPENSATION
In consideration of the Services to be performed pursuant to this Agreement, the Provider
will bill the Owner and the Owner agrees to pay Provider a not to exceed amount of One Hundred
Thirty Thousand Dollars (S130,000.00).Payment shall be based on work completed, delivered
and accepted by the Owner in accordance with the price quote contained in Attachment A, and
incorporated by reference as part of this agreement.Payment shall not bemade for anyrejected
photography or LiDARdata.Payment shall constitute full compensation for all work, defrayment
of all fees and other costs.Provider shall submit invoices to Owner upon completion of each
scheduled phase of the project as follows: 1) ground control survey services (approximately
$10,000); 2) aerial photography acquisition (approx. $36,400); 3) LiDAR acquisition (approx.
S54,600);4)imagery ortho rectification and delivery(approx.$11,600); and 5)LiDAR processing
